{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792272536,"nonce":"5PKQNlqxLGkCxsm0a3dNUX+tXAs=","title":"A link in a page does nothing: opening a URL needs a window command xwindow lacks","message":"**What**\n\nashui.ui.Anchor.open starts the system's opener as a process (open, explorer, xdg-open). A page can start no process, so in a web build (-D wasm) it now returns without doing anything: a click on `\u003ca href\u003e` is silent. A showcase site needs links to work.\n\n**Needed**\n\nA command from the program to the page, as xwindow's set title and set cursor are, that opens a URL (the page's window.open, or a navigation, with a target and noopener); xwindow's wire protocol lives in ash's docs/wasm/window.md and the xwindow core, with hlwindow the HashLink adapter. Then Anchor.open calls it on wasm. Opening has to happen inside the page's user gesture, as fullscreen and pointer lock do, so it should be deferred to the next pointerdown or keydown handler the same way.\n\n**Also**\n\nPlatform.current() is Web in a wasm build now.","files":null}]}